      156.45,
      443.69,
      433.87,
      468.35
    ],
    "text": "to amend the Employment of women, young persons and childrenAct, No. 47 of 1956",
    "fonts": [
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      244.39,
      173.23,
      366.67,
      182.3
    ],
    "text": "STATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT",
    "fonts": [
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      194.71,
      455.52,
      249.38
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2 : This clause amends section 3 of the Employment of Women, Young Personsand Children Act, No. 47 of 1956 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d)and the legal effect of that section as amended is to make reference to young persons whoare between the ages of sixteen and eighteen to be referred to as \u201cyoung persons\u201d inaccordance with the definition for \u201cyoung persons.\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      155.47,
      261.67,
      386.51,
      270.74
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3 : This clause is a consequential amendment to Clause 2.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      283.03,
      455.48,
      303.5
    ],
    "text": "Clause 4 : (1) This clause amends subsection (1) and sub section (2) of section 9 of theprincipal enactment and the legal effect of that section is-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      200.47,
      315.91,
      455.5,
      336.38
    ],
    "text": "(a)to increase the minimum age of employment in a vessel from fifteenyears to sixteen years.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      200.47,
      348.67,
      455.5,
      369.14
    ],
    "text": "(b)to increase the minimum age of employment in a school-ships andtraining-ships from fifteen years to sixteen years; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      381.43,
      455.52,
      401.9
    ],
    "text": "(2) Repeal subsection (3) of section 9 of the principal enactment and isconsequential to the amendments made to subsection (1) and subsection (2).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      414.31,
      455.53,
      434.78
    ],
    "text": "Clause 5 : This clause repeals section10 of the principal enactment and is a consequentialamendment to Clause 4.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      447.07,
      455.54,
      467.54
    ],
    "text": "Clause 6 : This clause amends section 20 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section is-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      194.47,
      479.83,
      455.47,
      500.3
    ],
    "text": "(a)to make reference to child and young person referrd to in subsection(1) in accordance with the definition for \u201cchild\u201d; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      194.47,
      512.71,
      455.51,
      544.58
    ],
    "text": "(b)to make reference to persons who has attained the age of fourteenyears but is under the age of eighteen years referred to in subsection(2) in accordance with the definition for \u201cyoung person.\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      194.47,
      556.87,
      455.49,
      588.74
    ],
    "text": "(c)to make reference to persons who has attained the age of sixteen yearsbut is under the age of eighteen years referred to in subsection (4) inaccordance with the definition for \u201cyoung person.\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      600.19,
      455.54,
      619.34
    ],
    "text": "Clause 7 : This clause amends section 34 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section as amended is-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      200.47,
      630.43,
      455.48,
      639.5
    ],
    "text": "(a) to amend the definitions of words \u201cchild\u201d, \u201cnight\u201d and \u201cyoung person\u201d:",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      200.47,
      650.47,
      455.5,
      669.62
    ],
    "text": "(b) to increase age of a person attending elementary school to be sixteenyears.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
